{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The governing distance figure is the trace, not the trip record. POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km decisive where the two disagree, and forbids citing trip_record.actual_distance_km for the threshold test. The trace measures 30.94 km against a booked optimal of 23.8 km: an excess of 7.14 km, which is 30.0% of the optimal distance. Both establishment limbs pass on their face - the excess is greater than 0.8 km and greater than 20% - and the derived deviation block records the status as 'established'. The deviation is therefore ESTABLISHED for this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02834", "EV-TRIP-02834"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08 is discharged on the face of the artifacts. The three artifacts that carry the claim - trip record, GPS trace and fare breakdown - all bear trip identifier TRP-02834, and the trace runs from the trip record's own start (10:10:16) to its own completion (10:50:36) within the recorded window. The excess (7.14 km, 30.0%) is measured from a trace that is unimpaired, with 100% coverage, 243 fixes and no gaps. The burden therefore shifts to the driver to point to a specific artifact and a specific clause for exoneration - a general assertion of good navigation does not discharge it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02834", "EV-GPS-02834", "EV-FARE-02834"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No rider instruction can be pressed against this claim. POL-RD-04 exonerates a deviation only to the extent it is attributable to a rider instruction recorded in the chat_log and corroborated by the trace, and POL-RD-14 addresses only instructions that were made and not followed. The chat log for TRP-02834 carries zero messages (message_count 0, first and last message timestamps null), and the trip record's chat_message_count is likewise 0. There is no instruction in existence, so no distance is excluded on that ground and the deviation stands at its measured figure.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02834", "EV-TRIP-02834"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-14"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's statement that he 'Followed navigation' is an assertion of an external cause that reaches no artifact. The only traffic_advisory in the bundle is EV-ADVIS-02834-01, and that artifact is IMPAIRED TO THE POINT OF ABSENCE: admissibility status MISSING, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight_multiplier 0.0, payload null, the pre-pass recording that no advisory covers the Northpoint City corridor in this window. I cite it for exactly that absence. Under POL-RD-13, POL-RD-03's comparison cannot be run on the record with no advisory covering the trip window, so POL-RD-03 is unavailable and the driver's excuse carries no weight under POL-RD-08. Because the driver names no evidence ID for any advisory, this is a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, and it does not escalate the case under POL-RD-10(5).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02834-01", "EV-GPS-02834"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is not impaired for policy purposes, so the rider's case does not depend on any corroborating source. POL-RD-07 impairs a trace only on a gap above 90 seconds, a straight-line jump above 500 m, or a sustained sampling interval above 30 seconds. This trace has a 10 second sample interval, max_gap_sec of 0.0, an empty gaps array and 100% coverage, so none of limbs (a) to (c) is met. The claim may rest on the trace alone, and the escalation route in POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02834"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The fare is metered, so the distance-and-time remedy is live. fare_breakdown.fare_model is METERED and quoted_fare_sgd is null. POL-RD-11 applies only where the fare model is UPFRONT_QUOTE with a non-null quoted fare, and it does not reach this trip; POL-RD-02 governs, and the rider's loss on distance and time is real rather than already absorbed at booking.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02834", "EV-TRIP-02834"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-11"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The refund is arithmetic under POL-RD-02, run on the booked optimal route because no exoneration or adjustment clause applies. Charged_total is 39.06. Recomputed fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 23.8 km optimal + 0.28 x 32.1 min optimal) x the surge multiplier of 1.0 read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier = 30.638, plus the 0.80 platform fee, plus zero ERP (no on-optimal-route gantry), plus no fixed surcharge, plus zero waiting time fee, less zero promo discount = 31.4380. Refund = 39.06 - 31.4380 = 7.6220, payable rounded up to SGD 7.65. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis, so no de minimis bar applies, and at 19.5% of charged_total it does not reach the 90% full-refund share, so the correct outcome on these lines is PARTIAL_REFUND. The computed figure of 7.65 exceeds the SGD 6.00 the rider put in issue, so the claim is made out in full and then some.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02834", "EV-TRIP-02834"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No pass-through line adds to or doubles the refund. The fare breakdown carries an empty erp_gantries list, tolls_erp of 0.00 and an off-optimal-route ERP total of 0.00, and there is no airport surcharge line. POL-RD-09(1) forbids adding off-route ERP on top of the POL-RD-02 figure, and here there is nothing to itemise in any event: the refund stands at the recomputation figure alone.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02834"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines.total",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Neither of the two clauses that would change the baseline applies. Under POL-RD-05 a relocation requires a non-null pickup_amended_at or dropoff_amended_at and a stored amended_optimal_distance_km; both amendment timestamps are null and amended_optimal_distance_km is null, so there is no amended endpoint and no re-quote, and the booked optimal stands. Under POL-RD-12 the matched-itinerary baseline exists only for RYDE_POOL trips; vehicle_type here is RYDE_X and solo_optimal_distance_km is null, so 23.8 km is the correct and only baseline against which the 30.94 km trace is measured.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02834"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-12"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider does not press the POL-RD-06 uplift and none is available, so the remedy stays at the POL-RD-02 figure. The deviation is not MATERIAL - 7.14 km is below the 8.0 km mark and 30.0% is below the 50% mark - so POL-RD-06's driver-profile check is not triggered at all. Were it run, neither limb of the pattern test is met: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0, well under 3, and 0 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 326 is 0, well under 0.05. The driver's lifetime prior_deviation_flags of 0 is not the trailing-90-day counter POL-RD-06 names, and POL-GEN-01 forbids substituting it. No conduct referral follows.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02834", "EV-GPS-02834"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own profile raises no gate. POL-RD-08's rider-side corroboration requirement bites only where rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 4 or more with substantiated claims of 1 or fewer; here deviation_claims_60d is 0 and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0, so the gate is not engaged and no corroboration beyond the trace is required. The rider's other profile fields - rating 4.84, 237 lifetime trips, prior disputes - are context only under POL-GEN-01 and may ground no finding either way.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-02834"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This case must be decided, not held. None of the POL-RD-10 triggers fires: the trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown; the trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07 and needs no corroboration; the timestamps run forward and agree; the refund of 7.65 is far below the SGD 150.00 ceiling and below charged_total; and every charge line is accounted for, with ERP and surcharge lines at zero. The only missing artifact, the traffic advisory cited at weight 0.0, is a gap in the bundle rather than the contradictory or invoked-against defect POL-RD-10(5) describes, as POL-RD-13 confirms. The disputed amount should be moved on this record, and because the monetary effect of 7.65 does not exceed the SGD 8.00 threshold in POL-GEN-05, it is executable on issue.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-02834", "EV-GPS-02834", "EV-FARE-02834", "EV-ADVIS-02834-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10", "POL-RD-13", "POL-GEN-05"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The only distance figure POL-RD-01 allows for the threshold test is the trace figure: gps_trace.trace_distance_km is 30.94 km against a booked optimal of 23.8 km, so the excess is 7.14 km and 30.0% (trip_record.actual_distance_km, 30.9, is a rounded convenience copy of the same measurement and may not be cited). That excess clears the establishment gate of 0.8 km and 20%, but it fails BOTH materiality limbs: 7.14 km is under the 8.0 km absolute figure and 30.0% is under the 50% proportional figure. This is therefore at most an ordinary established deviation; it cannot be uplifted to a FULL_REFUND of charged_total under POL-RD-06(b) and it cannot generate a POL-RD-06(c) driver-conduct referral.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02834", "EV-TRIP-02834"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No repeat-deviation pattern is established on the driver's own numbers: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 326, a ratio of 0.000, far below the 0.05 test POL-RD-06 sets, and nowhere near the 3-or-more-flags limb. The lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags is a different field and may not be substituted for the trailing-90-day figure; under POL-GEN-01 that counter, and every other profile field on this artifact (rating, acceptance_rate, lifetime_trips, cancellation_rate), is CONTEXT ONLY and can ground no finding against this driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02834"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace cannot be attacked as unfit to measure the excess: it carries 243 fixes at a 10.0 second sampling interval, which is exactly the expected interval, with 100.0% coverage, no gaps at all and a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds. None of POL-RD-07's limbs (a) to (c) is met, so the trace is not impaired for policy purposes and the escalation route in POL-RD-10(3) is not open on this record; the excess must be decided on this trace as measured.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02834"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver has no route-defence to run on this record and does not pretend otherwise. The chat log for the trip holds 0 messages, so POL-RD-04's rider-requested detour test has no instruction to test, no waypoint_hint to corroborate and no distance that can be excluded on that ground. Neither pickup_amended_at nor dropoff_amended_at is set and amended_optimal_distance_km and amended_optimal_duration_min are both null, so POL-RD-05 has no amended endpoint and no stored re-quote to apply. Vehicle_type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12's matched-itinerary baseline does not displace the booked optimal. The measured excess therefore stands as measured, and the dispute narrows to the remedy and to whether the money evidence is this trip's at all.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02834", "EV-TRIP-02834"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-12"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No traffic advisory covers this trip: EV-ADVIS-02834-01 is MISSING — status MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, no payload — so POL-RD-03's exoneration cannot be run on this record and no closure-adjusted optimal route exists. The driver's counter-statement says only 'Followed navigation'; it asserts no queue, breakdown, closure or incident and cites no advisory identifier, so nothing in it seeks POL-RD-03 exoneration. An assertion of that kind, unsupported by a traffic_advisory ID, discharges nothing under POL-RD-08. The missing artifact is cited here for its absence only, and the driver asks the judge to decide nothing from it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-02834-01", "EV-GPS-02834"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The money at stake is bounded by what the rider put in issue. The rider's quantified claim is $6.00, while the POL-RD-02 arithmetic on this ledger gives charged_total 39.06 less recomputed_fare 31.438 = 7.622, which rounds UP to 7.65. POL-GEN-03 defines PARTIAL_REFUND as the return of PART of the contested amount and FULL_REFUND as the return of the WHOLE of it; a refund cannot be larger than the sum the rider actually contested, so the ceiling on the rider-filed claim here is $6.00, not $7.65, and the driver's exposure is at most that sum.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02834"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-RD-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The fare breakdown does not carry this trip's identifier on its own face: the payload of EV-FARE-02834 records trip_id TRP-02734, while EV-TRIP-02834 and EV-GPS-02834 both record TRP-02834. POL-RD-08(a) makes matching trip identifiers across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown part of the rider's initial burden before any burden shifts, and POL-RD-10(2) forbids a final ruling and mandates escalation where those three do not all match. The pre-pass rating the artifact COMPLETE does not answer the point: POL-GEN-02(3) keeps schema-level assessment and policy-level assessment separate, and POL-RD-10(2) is a policy-level identifier test. On this record no refund should issue and the disputed sum should be held rather than paid out, with escalation naming POL-RD-10(2) as its trigger and a fare breakdown bearing this trip's identifier as what would resolve it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02834", "EV-TRIP-02834", "EV-GPS-02834"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-10", "POL-GEN-02", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{"ruling":{"ruling":"ESCALATE","amount_sgd":null,"driver_compensation_sgd":null,"referrals":[],"confidence":0.85,"explanation":"To both parties: this dispute cannot be finally decided on the record as it stands, so it goes to a human reviewer and the $6.00 in dispute is held — neither collected nor refunded.

