The rest of the record, so the reviewer has it. The deviation itself is established but not material: the trace measures 30.94 km against the booked optimal 23.8 km, an excess of 7.14 km (30.0%), which passes the POL-RD-01 gates of 0.8 km and 20% but is below the 8.0 km and 50% materiality marks, so no POL-RD-06 uplift and no conduct referral is available (the driver's deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 326 completed trips in 90 days in any event). The trace is not impaired for policy purposes — 243 fixes at 10 seconds, 100% coverage, no gaps, maximum gap 0.0 seconds — so POL-RD-07 and POL-RD-10(3) are not engaged. Nothing exonerates the excess: the chat log is empty (POL-RD-04 and POL-RD-14 have no instruction to test), no pickup or dropoff was amended and no amended optimal exists (POL-RD-05), the vehicle is RYDE_X so the pooled baseline of POL-RD-12 does not apply, and the only traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-02834-01, is MISSING with weight 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and the driver's 'Followed navigation' statement — which names no advisory and asserts no closure, queue or incident — discharges nothing under POL-RD-08. That absence does not itself escalate the case: under POL-RD-13 the missing advisory is a gap in the bundle, not the cited-artifact defect POL-RD-10(5) describes, because the driver cited no advisory at all. The fare is metered (fare_model METERED, quoted_fare_sgd null), so POL-RD-11 does not apply and the POL-RD-02 arithmetic would run as charged_total 39.06 less recomputed_fare 31.4380 = 7.6220, rounding up to 7.65 — above the SGD 0.50 de minimis, below the 90% full-refund share, and below the SGD 150.00 escalation ceiling. The driver's argument that any award is capped at the $6.00 contested, and the rider's contrary arithmetic of 7.65, are noted for the reviewer; no money moves now, because escalation under POL-RD-10 is terminal. No referral is issued: no clause produces one here (no POL-RD-06(c) pattern; no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity defect, the ERP and surcharge lines all being zero). Confidence is 0.85, capped by the weight-1.0 artifacts that carry the deciding identifier facts."},"discarded_claims":[{"claim":"This case must be decided, not held. None of the POL-RD-10 triggers fires: the trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown; the trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07 and needs no corroboration; the timestamps run forward and agree; the refund of 7.65 is far below the SGD 150.00 ceiling and below charged_total; and every charge line is accounted for, with ERP and surcharge lines at zero. The only missing artifact, the traffic advisory cited at weight 0.0, is a gap in the bundle rather than the contradictory or invoked-against defect POL-RD-10(5) describes, as POL-RD-13 confirms. The disputed amount should be moved on this record, and because the monetary effect of 7.65 does not exceed the SGD 8.00 threshold in POL-GEN-05, it is executable on issue.","side":"RIDER","reason_code":"IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED","detail":"the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02834-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"}]}

