    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute cannot be finally decided on the record as it stands, so it is escalated to a human reviewer under POL-RD-10(2). That escalation is terminal - it replaces any money outcome, no refund issues and no charge is collected, and the SGD 6.00 in dispute is held. Why. POL-RD-10(2) requires escalation where the trip identifiers on the trip record, the GPS trace and the fare breakdown do not all match. EV-TRIP-02834 and EV-GPS-02834 both carry trip TRP-02834. EV-FARE-02834 carries TRP-02834 on its face, but the ledger payload inside it records trip_id TRP-02734 - a different trip. The rider's assertion that all three artifacts bear TRP-02834 does not hold once the payload is read, and the pre-pass marking the artifact COMPLETE does not settle it, because POL-GEN-02(3) keeps the schema-level assessment separate from a policy-level identifier test. If the ledger names another trip, its figures (charged total 39.06, recomputed fare 31.4380) cannot safely move money. What would resolve it: a fare breakdown bearing TRP-02834, or a reconciliation from PAYMENTS_LEDGER. What is not in issue. The deviation is established on the trace: 30.94 km against the booked optimal 23.8 km is an excess of 7.14 km / 30.0%, clearing POL-RD-01's establishment gate (greater than 0.8 km and greater than 20%) but failing both materiality limbs (under 8.0 km and under 50%), so this is an ordinary established deviation, not a material one. The trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c) - 243 fixes, a 10-second interval, max gap 0.0 s, 100% coverage - so POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged and the rider may rest on the trace alone. With no material deviation, the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check and the POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral are unavailable; the profile in any event shows deviation_flags_90d 0 over 326 completed trips. The chat log holds 0 messages, no pickup or dropoff endpoint was amended, and the vehicle is RYDE_X, so POL-RD-04, POL-RD-05 and POL-RD-12 exclude nothing and POL-RD-14 has nothing to test. The only advisory in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-02834-01, is MISSING at weight_multiplier 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and is cited only for its absence; the driver's 'Followed navigation' names no advisory and asserts no external cause, so under POL-RD-13 that is a gap in the bundle rather than the POL-RD-10(5) trigger, and POL-RD-03 cannot be run. The money, for the reviewer. The fare model is METERED with quoted_fare_sgd null, so POL-RD-11 does not apply. POL-RD-02 gives recomputed fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 23.8 optimal km + 0.28 x 32.1 optimal min) x the surge multiplier 1.0 read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier, plus the 0.80 platform fee = 31.4380; refund = 39.06 - 31.4380 = 7.6220, rounded up to 7.65, above the 0.50 de minimis and below the 90% full-refund share. No ERP line or surcharge line exists, so POL-RD-09 adds nothing. The driver argues the rider's contested 6.00 caps any award; the rider argues the arithmetic stands and the claim is made out in full. Both points remain open for the reviewer. No amount is executed on an escalation, so the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold in POL-GEN-05 is not reached."
